# Reindex Test

`pebbles reindex` rebuilds .pebbles/index.json from the issue files: the
sanctioned repair for a conflicted or desynchronized index. This fixture has
an index missing one entry (the concurrent-new-issue loss), an unparsable
issue file, a file duplicating another file's id, and a file with keys
outside the Issue schema.

## Rebuild the index from the issue files

```console
$ PEBBLES_DB_PATH=.pebbles pebbles reindex
✓ Rebuilt index: 3 issue(s)
Warning: Skipped unparsable issue file broken-44444444-not-an-issue.json: missing 'id' field; it is not indexed
Warning: Skipped bug-55555555-dup-of-login.json: duplicate id (the first occurrence wins; this file is not indexed)

```

## Every issue still loads; schema violations are warned per load

The issue with unknown keys loads (degraded-but-usable) with a warning naming
the file and the keys; the unparsable and duplicate files stay unindexed.
The rebuilt index is order-preserving, but the list sorts by updated time.

```console
$ PEBBLES_DB_PATH=.pebbles pebbles list
Warning: Issue des-33333333-design-task.json has unknown key(s) not in the schema: assignee, priority; the file is loaded but the key(s) will be dropped on the next rewrite. Fix the file to remove them.
111 [bug] [TODO] Login bug ✓
222 [uc] [TODO] Second issue ✓
333 [des] [TODO] Design task ✓

```

## A healthy store is a no-op

```console
$ PEBBLES_DB_PATH=.pebbles pebbles reindex
✓ Index is up to date: 3 issue(s)
Warning: Skipped unparsable issue file broken-44444444-not-an-issue.json: missing 'id' field; it is not indexed
Warning: Skipped bug-55555555-dup-of-login.json: duplicate id (the first occurrence wins; this file is not indexed)

```
